  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Find the least number of times that a coin must be tossed to be at least 99% certain that you will obtain at least one head.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$7$ tosses.\n\nUse the probability of no heads, $(\\frac12)^n$, and compare $n=6$ and $n=7$.",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the number of independent tosses of a fair coin.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{at least one head})&=1-\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n\\\\1-\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n&\\ge\\frac{99}{100}\\\\\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n&\\le\\frac1{100}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac12\\right)^6&=\\frac1{64}>\\frac1{100}\\\\\\left(\\frac12\\right)^7&=\\frac1{128}<\\frac1{100}\\end{align*}$$\nThe probability of no heads decreases as $n$ increases, so the least number is $7$ tosses.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
